"""Readable report of the larger shared-input timing tier."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).parent;p=json.loads((root/'large_results/combined.json').read_text());summary=p['summary'];records=p['records'];fail=p['failures']
lines=['# Larger shared-grid regridding benchmarks','',f"Recorded {len(records)} repetitions across {len(summary)} successful grid/size/method profiles; {len(fail)} unsuccessful or incomplete profiles are retained in the raw JSON.",'', '**[Interactive report](https://lukegre.github.io/regridding-benchmarks/#large-timings)** · [Per-repeat CSV](large_results/measurements.csv) · [Full results](large_results/combined.json)','', '## Protocol','', '- Fixed shared source/destination geometries and scalar values within each grid/size profile; canonical hashes are verified before aggregation. Lossless native-format, longitude and storage-order adaptations are allowed.', '- Common 512 and 1024 scales across packages, plus a common 4096×4096 tier for all four CRS adapters. No per-package size tuning or padded execution time.', '- Three serial repetitions, one thread, two-vCPU / 8-GiB execution quota. Imports, small warmup, fixture generation and accuracy checks are outside the timers.', '- Setup and eager application are measured separately. Fused interfaces can build geometry/weights during application. CDO/Tempest/NCO native commands include process launch and native file I/O; Python file preparation/read costs are separately recorded.', '- MIR repeats use fresh processes and fresh cache directories. Original cached-call observations remain in `large_results/cache_controls/`.', '- Both WGS84 → Swiss LV95 and WGS84 → Web Mercator are included. Pure coordinate transforms are a separate comparison group from raster reprojection.', '- Reported values are arithmetic means and observed min/max of three runs, not confidence intervals. Different numerical kernels are not interchangeable.','', '## xarray-regrid extension', '', 'xarray-regrid 0.4.2 adds linear, nearest and conservative profiles on the existing rectilinear/full Gaussian grids. The xarray_axes control uses 1-D target coordinates instead of the historical xarray 2-D query arrays, without changing physical grids or values. Its public accessor constructs machinery/weights inside application; conservative meridian/parallel cells differ from ESMF great-circle cells. See [extension details](XARRAY_REGRID_REPORT.md).', '', '## Profile geometry','', '| Test | Scale | Source cells | Target cells |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
seen=set()
for r in summary:
 key=(r['comparison_group'],r['scale'])
 if key in seen:continue
 seen.add(key);lines.append(f"| {r['comparison_group']} | {r['scale']} | {r['source_cells']:,} | {r['target_cells']:,} |")
lines+=['','## Timings','', 'Times are seconds. `fused` means setup is API preparation and some weight/geometry work remains in application. NCO setup uses TempestRemap-generated weights.','', '| Test | Scale | Method | Mode | Setup mean | Apply mean | Total mean | Total range | RMSE | Finite |','| --- | ---: | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |']
for r in summary:
 err=f"{r['roundtrip_max_degrees']:.3g}° round-trip" if r['package']=='pyproj' else ('—' if r['rmse'] is None else f"{r['rmse']:.3g}")
 lines.append(f"| {r['comparison_group']} | {r['scale']} | {r['package']} | {r['timing_mode']} | {r['setup_seconds_mean']:.4f} | {r['apply_seconds_mean']:.4f} | {r['total_seconds_mean']:.4f} | {r['total_seconds_min']:.4f}–{r['total_seconds_max']:.4f} | {err} | {r['finite_fraction']:.2%} |")
lines+=['','## Limits','', 'The synthetic swath has incomplete coverage of its rectangular destination. Nearest-neighbour methods may fill points outside the swath footprint; bilinear and conservative methods have different support and missing-value behavior. Accuracy and coverage must be assessed alongside timings. Conservative inputs are analytic centre samples, not exact cell averages. The Xugrid profile is a separate projected, face-centred triangular mesh workflow. These are CPU single-field benchmarks, not memory stress tests, MPI scaling tests, or complete ROMS vector/vertical remapping.','']
if fail:
 lines+=['## Unsuccessful profiles','', 'Four TempestRemap/NCO profiles exceeded the 300-second limit in GenerateOverlapMesh, before weight generation/application completed. NCO uses the same TempestRemap setup, so these are not independent interpolation failures. They characterize this SCRIP-converted regional-overlap workflow; they do not establish a universal package limit. No interpolation speed is claimed for these profiles.','']
 for r in fail:lines.append(f"- {r['package']} / {r['grid']} / {r['scale']}: {r['status']}; {('GenerateOverlapMesh exceeded 300 seconds; no completed interpolation timing' if 'timed out after 300' in r.get('error','') else r.get('error','See raw record')[:300])}")
(root/'LARGE_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
print('Wrote LARGE_REPORT.md')
